            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naples34102"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I cut this recipe in half, as 1-1/2 ounces of liquor in a drink is plenty for me. Vanilla vodka is good. Amaretto, too...very nice. And Godiva white chocolate liqueur, which I used for this drink... wonderful. All of it thrown together with cranberry and pineapple juice is just... NOT good. Too sweet, too strong, strange flavor. Reminds me of my youth when everyone brought something to parties - it didn't really matter what and it was never \"the good stuff,\" dumped it into a big tub and had at it. We weren't particularly picky then.",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-20T09:00:55.880Z"
